<h2 id="antimass-deflectors"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Antimass_Deflectors">Antimass Deflectors</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The &minus;1 applies to space cannon rolls during both the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> and <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> steps.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player gains then loses the <i>Antimass Deflectors</i> technology, their units may remain in and move out of any <a href="/R_asteroid_field">asteroid fields</a> they are currently in, but cannot move additional units into or through.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="dark-energy-tap"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Dark_Energy_Tap">Dark Energy Tap</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A ship may be moved into the system containing the frontier token during the same action that it is explored.<sup>8</sup></li>
    <li>Exploring the frontier token happens at the end of the tactical action. Notably, this is after the <b>Space Cannon Offense</b> and/or <b>Space Combat</b> steps.<sup>2,8</sup></li>
    <li>Exploring the frontier token is mandatory if the player has a ship in the active system at the end of the tactical action.<sup>2,8</sup></li>
    <li>When a player gains <i>Dark Energy Tap</i>, they do not immediately explore any frontier tokens in systems containing their ships. They must activate those systems to explore those tokens.<sup>8</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If a player moves or places a ship into a system outside of a tactical action, they cannot explore a frontier token in that system.<sup>2,8</sup></li></ol>
    <li>The <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player cannot explore a frontier token with a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Technology#Faction_Technology:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a>. However, if they produce a ship during the <b>Production</b> step, they will be able to use that ship to explore the token.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>A player cannot use <i>Dark Energy Tap</i> to retreat into a system that contains another player&rsquo;s units, including ground forces and structures on planets.<sup>8</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="gravity-drive"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Gravity_Drive">Gravity Drive</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The +1 from <i>Gravity Drive</i> may be combined with the +1 from the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Flank%20Speed"><i>Flank Speed</i></a> action card, applying +2 to the move value of that ship.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="sling-relay"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Sling_Relay">Sling Relay</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The produced unit must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li><i>Sling Relay</i> cannot be used without producing a unit.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="fleet-logistics"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Fleet_Logistics">Fleet Logistics</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player may use the ability of <i>Fleet Logistics</i> the same turn they gain it.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s turn is ended by a game effect, they cannot use <i>Fleet Logistics</i> to perform an additional action.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>A player cannot use <i>Fleet Logistics</i> to pass on the same turn they performed an action.<sup>1</sup></li>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s second action would be to use a component action to play an action card, and that card is canceled, they are not required to perform an alternate second action on that turn.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player&rsquo;s first action is a strategic action, the other players resolve the secondary ability of that strategy card before the player performs their second action.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Effects that trigger at the start or end of a player&rsquo;s turn will not trigger between each of those player&rsquo;s actions.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="light-wave-deflector"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Propulsion_Technologies#Light/Wave_Deflector">Light/Wave Deflector</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A ship that uses <i>Light/Wave Deflector</i> to move through a system containing another player&rsquo;s ships may pick up and transport units from that system.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li><i>Light/Wave Deflector</i> does not allow a player to produce ships in a system that contains another player&rsquo;s ships.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="neural-motivator"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#Neural_Motivator">Neural Motivator</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Neural Motivator</i> only applies to the <b>Draw Action Card</b> step of the status phase. It does not apply to other effects that draw action cards, including but not limited to:<sup>1,5</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>The <a href="/R_politics"><i>Politics</i></a> strategy card.<sup>1,5</sup></li>
        <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Agenda_Cards#Directives:~:text=Minister%20of%20Policy"><i>Minister of Policy</i></a> law.<sup>1,5</sup></li>
        <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Exploration#Industrial_Exploration_Cards:~:text=Functioning%20Base"><i>Functioning Base</i></a> exploration card.<sup>1,5</sup></li>
        <li>The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Relics#Prophecy_of_Kings:~:text=The%20Prophet%27s%20Tears"><i>Prophet&rsquo;s Tears</i></a> relic.<sup>1,5</sup></li>
    </ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="psychoarchaeology"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#Psychoarchaeology">Psychoarchaeology</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Exhausting planets to gain trade goods can be done at any time during action phase, except when another ability is being resolved. For example, if a player has one of their planets with a technology specialty targeted with the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Uprising"><i>Uprising</i></a> action card, they cannot use <i>Psychoarchaeology</i> in response to gain a trade good.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    <li>If multiple planets are exhausted, the trade goods are gained one at a time.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

