<h2 id="x89-bacterial-weapon" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon">X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon</a> (replaced by &Omega;)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>10</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="x89-bacterial-weapon-omega" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon">X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</a> (replaced by &Omega;&Omega;)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega;&Omega; version.<sup>7</sup></li>
    <li><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</i> may be used against each planet in a system, if the conditions are met.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</i> will trigger only after all bombardment hits have been assigned.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The <a href="/F_lizix">L1Z1X</a> may use <i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</i> after they use their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_L1Z1X_Mindnet#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Harrow"><sc>Harrow</sc></a> faction ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li><i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;</i> cannot be used unless the player&rsquo;s <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> destroys at least one infantry; if all hits are assigned to mechs, it has no effect.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="x89-bacterial-weapon-omega-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Biotic_Technologies#X-89_Bacterial_Weapon">X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;&Omega;</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player with <i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;&Omega;</i> must mandatorily double the number of hits they produce.<sup>15</sup></li>
    <li>Effects that cancel hits will only cancel hits based on the doubled number of hits.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>Ground forces that are participating in space combat as though they were ships do not double the hits they produce.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol><li>Ships that are participating in ground combat as though they were ground forces double the hits they produce.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    <li>A player with <i>X&ndash;89 Bacterial Weapon &Omega;&Omega;</i> must mandatorily exhaust each planet they make a <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>bombardment</sc></a> roll against, even if they produce no hits.<sup>15</sup></li>
    <li>A player who bombards another player&rsquo;s coexisting units on a planet they control must still exhaust that planet.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>A war sun must target the same planet with all three of its <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>bombardment</sc></a> dice.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If a unit may roll additional <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>bombardment</sc></a> dice, such as by the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Plasma_Scoring"><i>Plasma Scoring</i></a> technology, that additional die must target the same planet.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>A player may roll for <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>bombardment</sc></a> against a planet that contains no ground forces.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="plasma-scoring"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Plasma_Scoring">Plasma Scoring</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>Only one additional dice is rolled for each bombardment or space cannon roll, regardless of how many units are using that ability.<sup>1,2,3</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>During an invasion in a system with multiple planets, only one unit will add a dice to its bombardment roll.<sup>1,2,6</sup></li>
        <li>During an invasion, if ground forces have been committed to multiple planets, <i>Plasma Scoring</i> will add an additional die to the space cannon rolls for each planet during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step.<sup>1</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>If a player makes separate <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> rolls against multiple coexisting players on the same planet, <i>Plasma Scoring</i> adds one additional die to only one of those rolls.<sup>6</sup></li>
    <li>A space dock using the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> ability due to the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Experimental%20Battlestation"><i>Experimental Battlestation</i></a> action card may roll an additional die from <i>Plasma Scoring</i>.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="ai-development-algorithm"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#AI_Development_Algorithm">AI Development Algorithm</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When a player exhausts <i>AI Development Algorithm</i> to ignore a prerequisite of a unit upgrade technology that they are researching, they may still use <i>AI Development Algorithm</i> itself for meeting a warfare technology (red) prerequisite on that unit upgrade technology in the same manner as any other technology.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>For example, <i>AI Development Algorithm</i> alone may be used to research the Destroyer II unit upgrade.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="magen-defense-grid" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid">Magen Defense Grid</a> (replaced by &Omega;)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega; version.<sup>10</sup></li>
    <li><i>Magen Defense Grid</i> cannot be used if all of a player&rsquo;s units in combat that had the <a href="/R_planetary_shield"><sc>Planetary Shield</sc></a> ability have lost it.<sup>2,3</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="magen-defense-grid-omega" class="removed"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid">Magen Defense Grid &Omega;</a> (replaced by &Omega;&Omega;)</h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>This card is replaced by the &Omega;&Omega; version.<sup>7</sup></li>
    <li>The player with <i>Magen Defense Grid &Omega;</i> chooses which ground force the hit is assigned to.<sup>10</sup></li>
    <li>The chosen ground force may cancel the hit by using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, if present. A different ground force with the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability cannot do so.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the last of a player&rsquo;s ground forces in a ground combat are destroyed by the effect of <i>Magen Defense Grid &Omega;</i>, that player loses the combat immediately. They will be unable to use any &ldquo;start of combat&rdquo; abilities.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The hit is produced at the start of ground combat, before any dice are rolled. A ground force destroyed by this hit does not roll.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="magen-defense-grid-omega-omega"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Magen_Defense_Grid">Magen Defense Grid &Omega;&Omega;</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The player with <i>Magen Defense Grid &Omega;&Omega;</i> chooses which ground force the hit is assigned to.<sup>15</sup></li>
    <li>The chosen ground force may cancel the hit by using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, if present. A different ground force with the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability cannot do so.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If the last of a player&rsquo;s ground forces in a ground combat are destroyed by the effect of <i>Magen Defense Grid &Omega;&Omega;</i>, that player loses the combat immediately. They will be unable to use any &ldquo;start of combat&rdquo; abilities.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li><i>Magen Defense Grid &Omega;&Omega;</i> will place infantry regardless of who activates the system.<sup>15</sup></li>
    <li>If a player has multiple structures in the system, one infantry is placed with each.<sup>15</sup></li>
    <li>The infantry must be placed on the same planet as the structure.<sup>15</sup></li>
    <ol><li>If the <a href="/F_saar">Saar</a> player owns <i>Magen Defense Grid &Omega;&Omega;</i>, and a system containing a <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Technology#Faction_Technology:~:text=Floating%20Factory">Floating Factory</a> is activated, then the infantry will be placed in the space area.<sup>*</sup></li></ol>
    </ol>

<h2 id="selfassembly-routines"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Self-Assembly_Routines">Self&ndash;Assembly Routines</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A mech cannot be placed in a space area with <i>Self&ndash;Assembly Routines</i>, and so cannot be placed in a system that does not contain a planet.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player wishes to place a mech, but there are none left in their reinforcements, they may remove a mech from any system that does not contain one of their command tokens and place that instead. The mech will be placed undamaged.<sup>1,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="duranium-armor"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Duranium_Armor">Duranium Armor</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player must mandatorily repair a unit with <i>Duranium Armor</i> during each round of combat, if possible.<sup>3</sup></li>
    <li>A player uses <i>Duranium Armor</i> only once during each round of combat, at the end of the <b>Assign Hits</b> substep. Hits assigned outside of this substep will not allow <i>Duranium Armor</i> to repair an additional unit.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li><i>Duranium Armor</i> is used even if a player&rsquo;s opponent produced no hits during a round of combat.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player starts a combat with a damaged unit, they use <i>Duranium Armor</i> in the first round of combat.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <ol><li>A player may use <i>Duranium Armor</i> to repair a unit damaged by <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> or <a href="/R_bombardment"><sc>Bombardment</sc></a> hits that occurred immediately before the combat.<sup>2</sup></li></ol>
    <li>If a unit is damaged during combat without using its <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability, it may be repaired by <i>Duranium Armor</i> during the same combat round.<sup>3</sup></li>
    <li>Only units participating in the combat may be chosen to be repaired.<sup>2,4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="assault-cannon"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Warfare_Technologies#Assault_Cannon">Assault Cannon</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>A player with <i>Assault Cannon</i> must mandatorily resolve its ability if they meet the requirement.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>If a player loses ships before they can resolve the <i>Assault Cannon</i> ability, they will be unable to resolve it if they no longer have three or more non&ndash;fighter ships.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>This will most commonly happen when both players in a combat have <i>Assault Cannon</i>, and the defender has exactly three non&ndash;fighter ships.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
        <li>Examples of other abilities that may remove units at the start of a space combat include the <a href="/F_creuss">Creuss</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Technology#Faction_Technology:~:text=Dimensional%20Splicer"><i>Dimensional Splicer</i></a> faction technology ability, the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Ambush"><sc>Ambush</sc></a> faction ability, the <a href="/F_yin">Yin</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Technology#Faction_Technology:~:text=Impulse%20Core"><i>Impulse Core</i></a> faction technology ability, as well as abilities such as the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Twilight_Imperium_Fourth_Edition:~:text=Courageous%20to%20the%20End"><i>Courageous to the End</i></a> action card or the <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Action_Cards#Codex_I:~:text=Reflective%20Shielding"><i>Reflective Shielding</i></a> action card that may trigger off of any of the previous abilities.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>A player may use an ability to add ships at the start of combat. If this brings the number of non&ndash;fighter ships to three or more, the player may then use the ability of <i>Assault Cannon</i>.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <ol>
        <li>Each other player may use one ability after that player has gained ships, and before that player has the opportunity to use the <i>Assault Cannon</i> ability. This may prevent that player from using the ability, as above.<sup>*</sup></li>
        <li>Examples of abilities that may add units at the start of space combat include a combination of the <a href="/F_mentak">Mentak</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Leaders:~:text=Sleeper%20Cell"><i>Sleeper Cell</i></a> hero ability and their <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Mentak_Coalition#Faction_Abilities:~:text=Ambush"><sc>Ambush</sc></a> faction ability, the ability of the <a href="/F_nekro">Nekro</a> player&rsquo;s flagship, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nekro_Virus#Flagship:~:text=The%20Alastor"><i>The Alastor</i></a>, and the <a href="/F_naaz_rokha">Naaz&ndash;Rokha</a> player&rsquo;s <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Naaz-Rokha_Alliance#Mech:~:text=Z-Grav%20Eidolon"><i>Eidolon</i></a> mech ability.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
    <li>Effects that cancel hits, such as <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a>, cannot be used to prevent ships from being destroyed.<sup>1,2,5</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="sarween-tools"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Sarween_Tools">Sarween Tools</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>If units are produced without any unit using its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability, <i>Sarween Tools</i> will not provide a reduction to the cost.<sup>1,2,3</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="scanlink-drone-network"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Scanlink_Drone_Network">Scanlink Drone Network</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The units must be on the planet before the <b>Movement</b> step of the tactical action.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="graviton-laser-system"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Graviton_Laser_System">Graviton Laser System</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li><i>Graviton Laser System</i> has no effect during the <b>Space Cannon Defense</b> step, as hits can only be assigned to ground forces.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>Hits produced while <i>Graviton Laser System</i> is in effect may still be canceled by the <a href="/R_sustain_damage"><sc>Sustain Damage</sc></a> ability.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li><i>Graviton Laser System</i> applies to every die rolled for the <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a> roll, including dice rolled by units using another unit&rsquo;s <a href="/R_space_cannon"><sc>Space Cannon</sc></a>, such as the <a href="/F_ral_nel">Ral Nel</a> player&rsquo;s Linkships.<sup>2</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="predictive-intelligence"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Predictive_Intelligence">Predictive Intelligence</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The ability of <i>Predictive Intelligence</i> to cast additional votes cannot be used if it is exhausted.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="transit-diodes"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Transit_Diodes">Transit Diodes</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>When resolving the ability of <i>Transit Diodes</i>, that player may remove ground forces from a system containing their command token.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The ground forces may be removed from on a planet or from in a space area.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The ground forces may be removed from different systems.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>The ground forces may be placed on different planets.<sup>*</sup></li>
    <li>If a mech is damaged when it is removed, it will remain damaged when it is placed.<sup>4</sup></li>
    </ol>

<h2 id="integrated-economy"><a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Integrated_Economy">Integrated Economy</a></h2>
    <ol class="note">
    <li>The produced units must be paid for.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li>There is no limit on the number of units produced, so long as the combined cost does not exceed the planet&rsquo;s resource value.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>A player explores a newly controlled planet before resolving <i>Integrated Economy</i>, so any attachment gained from that exploration affects the planet&rsquo;s resource value.<sup>2</sup></li>
    <li>A player may produce ships with <i>Integrated Economy</i>, unless another player has ships in the space area of that planet&rsquo;s system.<sup>2,5</sup></li>
    <li>No unit is using its <a href="/R_production"><sc>Production</sc></a> ability. The <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/Cybernetic_Technologies#Sarween_Tools"><i>Sarween Tools</i></a> technology and similar effects will not apply.<sup>1,2</sup></li>
    <li>Effects that let a player produce a unit for less than its cost, such as the <a href="/F_nomad">Nomad</a> player&rsquo;s commander, <a href="https://twilight-imperium.fandom.com/wiki/The_Nomad#Leaders:~:text=Navarch%20Feng">Navarch Feng</a>, do not change that unit&rsquo;s cost.<sup>*</sup></li>
    </ol>
</article>
